desktop-shell: battery and power mode on the taskbar

Left of the clock: the battery and its level on a laptop (cyan while
charging, a bolt on the charger, red at 10% or less on battery); on a
computer without a battery, a gauge showing the power mode. Hidden when
there is neither a battery nor a power mode to choose. The tooltip says
the level, the time left (or until full) and the power mode.

A click opens a menu: the battery level, the power modes (Power saver,
Balanced, Best performance; the current one highlighted), "Power
settings" (Settings, on its Power page) and "Shut down or restart..."
(hexa-power).

The battery comes from /sys/class/power_supply (batteries of peripherals,
scope "Device", are left out), read every few seconds; the power mode is
set by "hexa-power-mode set MODE" and read back from
/etc/hexaos/power-mode. The modes offered follow the same rules as
hexa-power-mode: all three with a platform profile or a CPU energy
preference, otherwise the ones the cpufreq governors allow.

